Market Overview
The Waste Paper and Pulp Recycling Market plays an important role in the transition toward a circular economy by converting discarded paper products into reusable fiber. Common feedstocks include post-consumer cartons, office paper, newsprint, and industrial paper offcuts. These materials pass through collection, sorting, pulping, de-inking, and refining processes before being used in new paper and packaging products.

Businesses are increasingly incorporating recycled fibers into their manufacturing processes to reduce dependence on virgin pulp and improve resource efficiency. Regulatory initiatives, corporate sustainability commitments, and demand for recyclable packaging are reinforcing this trend. The report identifies Asia-Pacific as a major market, supported by expanding industrial activity and growing demand for recycled materials.

